@@ -28,0 +29,24 @@ A local build does not prove deployment or live Twitch sign-in.
+
+## Shared scope snapshot
+
+The canonical source is the plugin's `src/auth/permissions.ts`.
+`lib/twitch/permissions.generated.json` holds its scope and consent data.
+The file records the source path and SHA-256. It is a generated snapshot,
+not a second hand-maintained policy. Runtime and tests use this local file.
+They do not need the plugin checkout on the hosted server.
+
+Run the sync check from this Site while authoring in the parent checkout:
+
+```sh
+bun scripts/sync-twitch-permissions.ts ../../src/auth/permissions.ts --check
+```
+
+To refresh it, omit `--check`. A separate checkout can pass an absolute
+canonical source path. The script imports that source only at authoring time.
+No sync check is needed when building a standalone published Site checkout.
+
+The request is the sorted union of the baseline, prior grants, and extra
+scopes. Token validation must contain all requested scopes before save.
+Denied or incomplete reauthorization keeps the previous connection.
+A rejected new token is revoked unless it is the current saved token.
+Existing zero-scope grants stay connected but need fresh consent.
